{
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.work": "The world of work",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.work.texto": "When you apply for a job, you send a CV (résumé) and a cover letter. In the interview you talk about your skills, your experience and why you want the position.\n\n\"I have worked as a waiter for two years.\" \"I am good at teamwork.\" \"I would like to grow in this company.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.1": "What is a CV?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.1.a": "A document with your education and work experience",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.1.b": "A type of contract",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.1.c": "A salary",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.1.por_que": "Also called a résumé.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.2": "\"I have worked here ___ two years.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.2.a": "since",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.2.b": "for",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.2.c": "ago",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.2.por_que": "For + period of time.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.3": "\"I have lived in Santiago ___ 2019.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.3.a": "for",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.3.b": "during",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.3.c": "since",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.3.por_que": "Since + starting point.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.4": "What does \"teamwork\" mean?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.4.a": "Working well with other people",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.4.b": "Working alone",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.4.c": "Working at night",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.4.por_que": "Team + work.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.5": "Which is a good interview answer?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.5.a": "I don't know.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.5.b": "I am responsible and I learn fast.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.5.c": "I hate working.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.5.por_que": "Show your strengths.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.6": "What is a \"cover letter\"?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.6.a": "A letter of complaint",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.6.b": "A bill",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.6.c": "A letter that explains why you want the job",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.6.por_que": "It goes with your CV.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.7": "\"Salary\" means:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.7.a": "The money you earn for working",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.7.b": "A vacation",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.7.c": "A boss",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.7.por_que": "Usually paid monthly.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.8": "\"I would like ___ in your company.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.8.a": "working",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.8.b": "to work",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.8.c": "work",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.8.por_que": "Would like + to + verb.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.9": "What does \"deadline\" mean?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.9.a": "A dangerous line",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.9.b": "A day off",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.9.c": "The last day to finish something",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.9.por_que": "Don't miss it.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.10": "\"She is in charge of the team.\" means:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.10.a": "She is responsible for the team",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.10.b": "She pays the team",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.10.c": "She left the team",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.work.10.por_que": "In charge = responsible.",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.reported": "Reported speech",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.reported.texto": "Reported speech tells what someone said without quoting exactly. The verb usually goes one step back in time:\n\n\"I am tired,\" she said. → She said (that) she was tired.\n\"I will call you,\" he said. → He said he would call me.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.1": "\"I am happy,\" Ana said. → Ana said she ___ happy.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.1.a": "was",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.1.b": "is",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.1.c": "were",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.1.por_que": "Present → past.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.2": "\"I will help,\" Tom said. → Tom said he ___ help.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.2.a": "will",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.2.b": "would",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.2.c": "won't",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.2.por_que": "Will → would.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.3": "\"I can swim,\" he said. → He said he ___ swim.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.3.a": "can",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.3.b": "may",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.3.c": "could",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.3.por_que": "Can → could.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.4": "\"I like pizza,\" she said. → She said she ___ pizza.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.4.a": "liked",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.4.b": "likes",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.4.c": "like",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.4.por_que": "Present simple → past simple.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.5": "Which verb is common in reported speech?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.5.a": "go",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.5.b": "said",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.5.c": "eat",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.5.por_que": "Also \"told\".",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.6": "\"He told ___ he was late.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.6.a": "to me that said",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.6.b": "I",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.6.c": "me",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.6.por_que": "Tell + person.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.7": "\"We are studying,\" they said. → They said they ___ studying.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.7.a": "were",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.7.b": "are",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.7.c": "was",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.7.por_que": "Are → were.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.8": "\"I have finished,\" she said. → She said she ___ finished.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.8.a": "has",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.8.b": "had",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.8.c": "have",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.8.por_que": "Present perfect → past perfect.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.9": "Reported question: \"Where do you live?\" → He asked me where I ___.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.9.a": "live",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.9.b": "do live",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.9.c": "lived",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.9.por_que": "No question order.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.10": "\"Don't run!\" the teacher said. → The teacher told us ___ run.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.10.a": "not to",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.10.b": "don't",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.10.c": "to not to",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.reported.10.por_que": "Negative order: not to + verb.",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.future": "Plans and the future",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.future.texto": "We use \"going to\" for plans and \"will\" for decisions in the moment or predictions. For fixed arrangements we often use the present continuous.\n\n\"I'm going to study medicine.\" \"It will rain tomorrow.\" \"I'm meeting Sofía at six.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.1": "\"I ___ study engineering next year.\" (a plan)",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.1.a": "am going to",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.1.b": "will be went",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.1.c": "going",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.1.por_que": "Going to for plans.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.2": "\"It's cold. I ___ close the window.\" (decision now)",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.2.a": "am going",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.2.b": "will",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.2.c": "was",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.2.por_que": "Will for quick decisions.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.3": "\"I'm meeting my friend at six.\" expresses:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.3.a": "A past habit",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.3.b": "An order",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.3.c": "A fixed arrangement",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.3.por_que": "Present continuous for arrangements.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.4": "\"I think it ___ rain.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.4.a": "will",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.4.b": "is",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.4.c": "was",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.4.por_que": "Predictions with will.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.5": "Negative: \"I ___ going to travel.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.5.a": "not am",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.5.b": "am not",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.5.c": "don't",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.5.por_que": "Am not going to.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.6": "\"Will you help me?\" is:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.6.a": "A past action",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.6.b": "A command in the past",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.6.c": "A request",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.6.por_que": "Asking for help.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.7": "\"By 2030 I ___ have finished university.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.7.a": "will",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.7.b": "am",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.7.c": "did",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.7.por_que": "Future perfect: will have + participle.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.8": "\"Are you going to ___ the exam?\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.8.a": "taking",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.8.b": "take",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.8.c": "took",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.8.por_que": "Going to + base form.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.9": "Which sentence talks about the future?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.9.a": "We saw.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.9.b": "We see every day.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.9.c": "We will see.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.9.por_que": "Will = future.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.10": "\"I hope ___ a good job.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.10.a": "to get",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.10.b": "get",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.10.c": "getting to",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.future.10.por_que": "Hope + to + verb.",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.society": "Technology and society",
  "tema.chile.ingles.m4.society.texto": "Technology changes how we live: social media, artificial intelligence and online shopping. It brings benefits but also risks, like misinformation and privacy problems.\n\nUseful phrases: \"On the one hand..., on the other hand...\", \"In my opinion...\", \"However...\".",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.1": "\"On the one hand... on the other hand\" is used to:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.1.a": "Compare two sides of an idea",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.1.b": "Count numbers",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.1.c": "Say goodbye",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.1.por_que": "Balanced argument.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.2": "What is \"privacy\"?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.2.a": "A public party",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.2.b": "Keeping your personal information safe",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.2.c": "A type of phone",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.2.por_que": "Protect your data.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.3": "\"However\" means:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.3.a": "Because",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.3.b": "Also",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.3.c": "But / nevertheless",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.3.por_que": "Introduces a contrast.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.4": "What is \"misinformation\"?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.4.a": "False or wrong information",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.4.b": "A school subject",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.4.c": "A news channel",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.4.por_que": "Check sources.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.5": "\"AI\" stands for:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.5.a": "Automatic internet",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.5.b": "Artificial intelligence",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.5.c": "Active idea",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.5.por_que": "Machines that learn.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.6": "\"In my opinion, social media ___ addictive.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.6.a": "can is",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.6.b": "be can",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.6.c": "can be",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.6.por_que": "Modal + base verb.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.7": "Which is an advantage of technology?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.7.a": "Faster communication",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.7.b": "More pollution only",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.7.c": "Less information",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.7.por_que": "Instant messages.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.8": "\"Download\" means:",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.8.a": "To delete a file",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.8.b": "To copy a file from the internet to your device",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.8.c": "To turn off",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.8.por_que": "Opposite: upload.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.9": "\"If I had more time, I ___ learn to code.\"",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.9.a": "will",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.9.b": "am",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.9.c": "would",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.9.por_que": "Second conditional.",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.10": "What does \"screen time\" mean?",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.10.a": "Time spent using devices with screens",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.10.b": "Movie hours",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.10.c": "TV schedule",
  "pregunta.chile.ingles.m4.society.10.por_que": "Phones, tablets, PCs."
}
